.TH SQLITE3-CONFIG 3 "October 2026" "go-dhcpd 1.8.0" "go-dhcpd Plugin Interface"
.SH NAME
sqlite3-config \- read/write go-dhcpd config-provider plugin backed by a SQLite3 database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I <install_prefix>/lib/go-dhcpd/plugins/sqlite3-config.plugin
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sqlite3-config
is a go-dhcpd config-provider plugin, not a standalone command-line
program.
.B "It is not meant to be run directly from a shell."
It is spawned as a subprocess by
.BR dhcpd (8)
once per request: the daemon writes one JSON-encoded request to the
plugin's standard input and closes it, the plugin writes one
JSON-encoded response to standard output, and the process exits. See
.B PROTOCOL
below for the exact message shapes.
.PP
If
.B sqlite3-config
is executed interactively (standard input attached to a terminal), it
prints a warning explaining that it is a plugin and exits with status 1
instead of blocking on input; see
.B DIAGNOSTICS
below.
.PP
Unlike
.BR go\-dhcpd\-file\-config (3),
.B sqlite3-config
is a
.BR "full-featured, read/write plugin" :
it stores subnet and static-host definitions in a SQLite3 database
(named by the
.B db_path
setting, see
.BR CONFIGURATION )
instead of a JSON5 configuration file, and implements every
create/read/update/delete action defined by the protocol. This lets the
go-dhcpd REST API's
.B /subnets
and
.B /static
endpoints perform normal CRUD operations against the data this plugin
manages, rather than returning
.BR "403 Forbidden" .
Existing
.B subnets
/
.B static
data can be moved out of a
.BR config.json5 (5)
file and into a database usable by this plugin with
.BR go\-dhcpd\-migration\-tool (8).
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B sqlite3-config
is selected and configured through
.B plugins.config_provider
in
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5):
.PP
.RS
.nf
"plugins": {
  "config_provider": {
    "name": "sqlite3-config",
    "settings": { "db_path": "/var/lib/go-dhcpd/networks.db" }
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR db_path " (string, settings key, required)"
Path to the SQLite3 database file. Created automatically, along with
its schema, the first time the plugin opens it if it does not already
exist.
.SH PROTOCOL
Each invocation reads exactly one JSON request object from standard
input:
.TP
.B version
(integer) Protocol version; currently always 1.
.TP
.B action
(string) The operation requested; see
.B ACTIONS
below.
.TP
.B settings
(object) The plugin's configured settings, copied from
.B plugins.config_provider.settings
(see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
.TP
.B data
(object, action-specific) Request payload: a subnet or static-host
object for add/update actions, or an identifying field for delete
actions; see
.B ACTIONS
below.
.PP
Exactly one JSON response object is written to standard output:
.TP
.B status
(string) One of
.BR success ", " error ", or " validation_error .
.B validation_error
marks a rejection caused by invalid request data (missing/malformed
fields, bad MAC address, non-IPv4 literal, etc.); the go-dhcpd REST API
maps it to a 4xx response, as opposed to
.BR error \'s
5xx (execution/storage failures).
.TP
.B message
(string, on error/validation_error) A human-readable description of
the failure.
.TP
.B data
(any, on success) Action-specific result payload.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B capabilities
Returns
.BR name ", " version ", and " writable
(always
.BR true ).
.TP
.B get_subnets
Returns every stored subnet, in the shape documented under
.B SUBNETS
in
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5).
.TP
.BR add_subnet " / " update_subnet
.B data
is a subnet object (see
.B SUBNETS
in
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5)).
Validated (network/netmask/dynamic-range/server-list fields must be
valid IPv4) before being inserted or replacing the existing subnet with
the same
.BR network .
.B update_subnet
fails if no subnet with that
.B network
exists.
.TP
.B delete_subnet
.B data
is
.RB { \(dq network\(dq : " " \(dq...\(dq }.
Fails if no subnet with that
.B network
exists.
.TP
.B get_static_hosts
Returns every stored static host, ordered by MAC address, in the shape
documented under
.B STATIC
in
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5).
.TP
.BR add_static_host " / " update_static_host
.B data
is a static-host object (see
.B STATIC
in
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5)).
.B mac_address
must be a valid 6-byte Ethernet address (canonicalized and used as the
lookup key) and
.B ip_address
must be non-empty.
.B update_static_host
fails if no static host with that
.B mac_address
exists.
.TP
.B delete_static_host
.B data
is
.RB { \(dq mac_address\(dq : " " \(dq...\(dq }.
Fails if no static host with that
.B mac_address
exists.
.PP
Any other
.B action
value is rejected with a
.B status
of
.B error
and an "unknown action" message.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
When standard input is a terminal (i.e. the binary was launched
directly by a user rather than by
.BR dhcpd (8)),
.B sqlite3-config
prints:
.PP
.RS
.nf
This binary is a go-dhcpd plugin (sqlite3-config).
These are not meant to be executed directly.
Please run go-dhcpd itself, which will invoke this plugin automatically.
.fi
.RE
.PP
to standard error and exits with status 1, without attempting to read a
request.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/go-dhcpd/plugins/sqlite3-config.plugin
Default install location (actual prefix depends on
.B INSTALL_PREFIX
used at build/install time; see
.BR dhcpd (8)).
.TP
.IR db_path " (configured, see " CONFIGURATION )
SQLite3 database holding the
.B subnets
and
.B static_hosts
tables and their child tables; schema shared with
.BR go\-dhcpd\-migration\-tool (8).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dhcpd (8),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-file\-config (3),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-migration\-tool (8)
